        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Gaugamela</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">1 October 331 BCE, by calculation from the lunar eclipse of 20 to 21 September of that year</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Gaugamela, a village on the river Bumodus north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erbil">Arbela</a> (modern Erbil) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> Plains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>; the exact site is not known, and Karamlesh is the most commonly accepted</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> with Greek allies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arrian">Arrian</a> gives 7,000 cavalry and 40,000 infantry, figures modern scholars generally accept) against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, whose army ancient sources put at up to 1,000,000 and modern estimates at about 91,000 to 120,000, with no agreed figure</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius</a> fled the field and the Persian army broke up; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> and Darius was later murdered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessus">Bessus</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>.</span></div>
