    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Ancient writers give the Persian army as up to a million men, figures modern historians call absurd or of no use; modern estimates run from about 91,000 to 120,000.</li><li>The site of the battle is not known with certainty, and the date of 1 October 331 BCE is a calculation from an eclipse reported by ancient sources.</li><li>After the battle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius</a> fled east and was killed by his own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessus">Bessus</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> is traditionally considered to have ended with his death.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a> offered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander</a> all territory west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, his daughter in marriage and 30,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talent">talents</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> before the battle, according to Diodorus, Curtius and Justin; Alexander refused.</p></aside>
    </section>

